{"schema": 1, "provider": "codex", "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "request_sha256": "0bba4b752c349b534b42e8689fc4b523392e2c99cde63166e1679566207ba3fb", "invocation_metadata": {"schema": 1, "image_id": "sha256:79462fb575e55c574c60e95256406443339fd0aebddbaddec572b8d1b632ae39", "executable_path": "/usr/local/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/bin/codex.js", "executable_sha256": "61b0194f3bb6534439c8d26a3ed57d0805f84b884588b761795323eeb92fcf70", "known_configuration_path": "/home/codex/.codex/config.toml", "known_configuration_sha256": "c8597a1fbc447e945c45fc00126a131d9c3a824d2e6f96a57288de382363b87a", "other_effective_configuration": "unknown; trusted launcher/profile boundary", "response_schema_sha256": "374d4bb692012196f95c8105308100b0aeebe7a8fcc28fcb12010183313548a8", "response_schema_scope": "Prompt guidance and strict local validation only; no provider enforcement claim", "public_model_catalog_sha256": "fd219bd9f061278275f528939f82f54d2eb97df4b25c23b022adbe48813d920b", "runtime_model_catalog_sha256": "5f16461bf0477c6e522b6cdbb66d627a246e0da675721fe8cb8b35163cb736c9", "tool_surface_override": "direct; no shell, patch, search or experimental tools", "requested_reasoning_effort": "medium", "effective_remote_reasoning_effort": "not observed", "effective_features": {"disabled_features": ["apps", "plugins", "remote_plugin", "hooks", "daemon_auto_start", "shell_tool", "code_mode_host", "browser_use", "browser_use_external", "browser_use_full_cdp_access", "computer_use", "in_app_browser", "image_generation", "view_image", "multi_agent", "multi_agent_v2", "skill_search", "sleep_tool", "goals", "tool_suggest", "workspace_dependencies", "request_permissions_tool", "agent_message_board"], "unified_exec_observed": true, "shell_registration_control": "shell_tool=false; Codex 0.160.0 spec_plan.rs", "complete_configuration_isolation": false}}, "native_exit_code": 0, "usage_reported": {"input_tokens": 32627, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "cache_write_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 5638, "reasoning_output_tokens": 125}, "native_reconnections": [], "result": {"schema": 1, "reason": "Se suministra el archivo fijo de pruebas y una nota nueva de cobertura, con fixtures incorporados y carga por ruta absoluta. No se modifican el programa, README ni documentos originales. No se afirma ejecución ni resultado de pruebas.", "documents": {}, "files": {"test_topo_plan.py": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Stdlib contract battery; fixtures are constructed entirely in memory.\"\"\"\nimport contextlib\nimport copy\nimport io\nimport itertools\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport random\nimport runpy\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport unittest\n\nPROGRAM = str(Path(__file__).resolve().with_name('topo_plan.py'))\nLIMIT = 131072\nERROR = b'topo-plan: invalid input\\n'\nEMPTY = {'nodes': [], 'edges': []}\n\n\ndef encode(value):\n    return json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=True, separators=(',', ':')).encode('ascii')\n\n\ndef oracle(request):\n    \"\"\"Direct predecessor inspection, independent of heap/indegree algorithms.\"\"\"\n    predecessors = {node: set() for node in request['nodes']}\n    for source, target in request['edges']:\n        predecessors[target].add(source)\n    remaining = set(predecessors)\n    order = []\n    while remaining:\n        ready = {node for node in remaining if not predecessors[node].intersection(remaining)}\n        if not ready:\n            raise ValueError('cycle')\n        chosen = min(ready)\n        order.append(chosen)\n        remaining.remove(chosen)\n    remaining = set(predecessors)\n    layers = []\n    while remaining:\n        ready = sorted(node for node in remaining if not predecessors[node].intersection(remaining))\n        if not ready:\n            raise ValueError('cycle')\n        layers.append(ready)\n        remaining.difference_update(ready)\n    return {'order': order, 'layers': layers, 'roots': layers[0][:] if layers else []}\n\n\ndef unique_object(pairs):\n    result = {}\n    for key, value in pairs:\n        if key in result:\n            raise ValueError('duplicate output key')\n        result[key] = value\n    return result\n\n\ndef reject_constant(value):\n    raise ValueError('nonfinite output')\n\n\nclass NoRead:\n    @property\n    def buffer(self):\n        return self\n\n    def read(self, *args):\n        raise AssertionError('import read stdin')\n\n\nclass ShortReader:\n    def __init__(self, data, width):\n        self.data = data\n        self.width = width\n        self.position = 0\n        self.requests = []\n\n    def read(self, size):\n        self.requests.append(size)\n        end = min(len(self.data), self.position + min(size, self.width))\n        chunk = self.data[self.position:end]\n        self.position = end\n        return chunk\n\n\nclass TopoPlanTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    @classmethod\n    def setUpClass(cls):\n        out, err = io.StringIO(), io.StringIO()\n        original = sys.stdin\n        try:\n            sys.stdin = NoRead()\n            with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out), contextlib.redirect_stderr(err):\n                cls.module = runpy.run_path(PROGRAM, run_name='topo_plan_battery')\n        finally:\n            sys.stdin = original\n        if out.getvalue() or err.getvalue():\n            raise AssertionError('import emitted output')\n\n    def invoke(self, data):\n        script = 'import runpy; runpy.run_path(' + repr(PROGRAM) + ', run_name=\"__main__\")'\n        return subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-I', '-B', '-c', script], input=data,\n                              stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\n                              timeout=5, check=False)\n\n    def valid(self, data, expected):\n        result = self.invoke(data)\n        self.assertTrue(result.returncode == 0, 'valid batch exit differs')\n        self.assertTrue(result.stderr == b'', 'valid batch emitted stderr')\n        if not expected:\n            self.assertTrue(result.stdout == b'', 'zero requests emitted output')\n            return\n        self.assertTrue(result.stdout.endswith(b'\\n'), 'missing final LF')\n        lines = result.stdout[:-1].split(b'\\n')\n        self.assertTrue(len(lines) == len(expected), 'response framing/count differs')\n        for index, (line, wanted) in enumerate(zip(lines, expected)):\n            actual = json.loads(line.decode('utf-8'), object_pairs_hook=unique_object,\n                                parse_constant=reject_constant)\n            self.assertTrue(type(actual) is dict, 'response is not an object')\n            self.assertTrue(set(actual) == {'order', 'layers', 'roots'}, 'response keys differ')\n            self.assertTrue(type(actual['order']) is list and type(actual['roots']) is list,\n                            'order/roots must be lists')\n            self.assertTrue(type(actual['layers']) is list, 'layers must be a list')\n            self.assertTrue(all(type(layer) is list for layer in actual['layers']),\n                            'round must be a list')\n            flat = actual['order'] + actual['roots'] + list(itertools.chain.from_iterable(actual['layers']))\n            self.assertTrue(all(type(node) is str for node in flat), 'response node type differs')\n            self.assertTrue(actual == wanted, 'response mismatch at index %d' % index)\n\n    def invalid(self, data):\n        result = self.invoke(data)\n        self.assertTrue(result.returncode == 2, 'invalid input exit differs')\n        self.assertTrue(result.stdout == b'', 'invalid batch emitted output')\n        self.assertTrue(result.stderr == ERROR, 'invalid input diagnostic differs')\n\n    def requests(self, requests):\n        self.valid(b'\\n'.join(encode(r) for r in requests) + b'\\n', [oracle(r) for r in requests])\n\n    def test_public_examples(self):\n        fixtures = [\n            ({'nodes': ['z', 'b', 'a'], 'edges': [['a', 'b']]},\n             {'order': ['a', 'b', 'z'], 'layers': [['a', 'z'], ['b']], 'roots': ['a', 'z']}),\n            ({'nodes': ['c', 'a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'c'], ['b', 'c'], ['a', 'c']]},\n             {'order': ['a', 'b', 'c'], 'layers': [['a', 'b'], ['c']], 'roots': ['a', 'b']}),\n            (EMPTY, {'order': [], 'layers': [], 'roots': []})]\n        self.valid(b'\\n'.join(encode(r) for r, _ in fixtures) + b'\\n', [e for _, e in fixtures])\n        self.requests([\n            {'nodes': ['a'], 'edges': []},\n            {'nodes': ['z', 'aa', 'a_', 'a0', 'a'], 'edges': []},\n            {'nodes': ['d', 'c', 'b', 'a'], 'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['b', 'c'], ['c', 'd']]},\n            {'nodes': ['e', 'd', 'c', 'b', 'a'], 'edges': [['a', 'c'], ['b', 'c'], ['c', 'd'], ['c', 'e']]},\n            {'nodes': ['z', 'y', 'c', 'b', 'a'], 'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['y', 'z']]},\n            {'nodes': ['z', 'd', 'c', 'b', 'a'], 'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['b', 'c'], ['a', 'd']]}])\n\n    def test_exhaustive_small_graphs(self):\n        names = ['a', 'b', 'c']\n        edges = [(a, b) for a in names for b in names if a != b]\n        dags = []\n        for mask in range(64):\n            request = {'nodes': names[::-1], 'edges': [list(e) for i, e in enumerate(edges) if mask & (1 << i)]}\n            try:\n                oracle(request)\n            except ValueError:\n                with self.subTest(cyclic_mask=mask):\n                    self.invalid(encode(request))\n            else:\n                dags.append(request)\n        self.requests(dags)\n        batch = []\n        for permutation in itertools.permutations(['a', 'b', 'c', 'd']):\n            edges = list(itertools.combinations(permutation, 2))\n            for mask in range(64):\n                batch.append({'nodes': list(reversed(permutation)),\n                              'edges': [list(e) for i, e in enumerate(edges) if mask & (1 << i)]})\n                if len(batch) == 80:\n                    self.requests(batch)\n                    batch = []\n        if batch:\n            self.requests(batch)\n\n    def test_generated_dags_and_permutations(self):\n        rng = random.Random(18473)\n        batch = []\n        for size in range(1, 13):\n            for _ in range(4):\n                names = ['n%02d' % i for i in range(size)]\n                rng.shuffle(names)\n                base = {'nodes': names, 'edges': [list(e) for e in itertools.combinations(names, 2) if rng.random() < 0.3]}\n                expected = oracle(base)\n                for variant in range(3):\n                    request = copy.deepcopy(base)\n                    rng.shuffle(request['nodes'])\n                    request['edges'] += copy.deepcopy(request['edges'][:variant + 1])\n                    rng.shuffle(request['edges'])\n                    self.assertTrue(oracle(request) == expected, 'fixture graph changed')\n                    batch.append(request)\n                    if len(batch) == 40:\n                        self.requests(batch)\n                        batch = []\n        if batch:\n            self.requests(batch)\n\n    def test_independent_graph_state(self):\n        request = {'nodes': ['z', 'd', 'c', 'b', 'a'], 'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['a', 'b'], ['b', 'c'], ['a', 'd']]}\n        original = copy.deepcopy(request)\n        adjacency, indegree = self.module['normalize_graph'](request)\n        saved = copy.deepcopy((adjacency, indegree))\n        expected = oracle(request)\n        for _ in range(3):\n            for function, key in [('topological_order', 'order'), ('topological_layers', 'layers'),\n                                  ('topological_layers', 'layers'), ('topological_order', 'order')]:\n                self.assertTrue(self.module[function](adjacency, indegree) == expected[key], 'repeated calculation differs')\n                self.assertTrue((adjacency, indegree) == saved, 'planner mutated base graph')\n            result = self.module['plan_request'](request)\n            self.assertTrue(result == expected, 'plan_request differs')\n            self.assertTrue(request == original, 'request mutated')\n            result['roots'].append('sentinel')\n            self.assertTrue(result['layers'] == expected['layers'], 'roots aliases first layer')\n\n    def test_schema_names_and_edge_types(self):\n        cases = [None, True, 1, 'x', [], [EMPTY], {}, {'nodes': []}, {'edges': []},\n                 {'nodes': [], 'edges': [], 'extra': 0}]\n        for value in [None, True, 3, 'a', {}, {'a': 1}]:\n            cases += [{'nodes': value, 'edges': []}, {'nodes': [], 'edges': value}]\n        for name in ['', 'A', '0a', '_a', 'a-b', 'a.b', 'a b', 'a\\n', 'a\\r', 'a\\x00',\n                     'é', 'ａ', 'a' * 17, None, True, 2, [], {}]:\n            cases.append({'nodes': [name], 'edges': []})\n        cases.append({'nodes': ['a', 'a'], 'edges': []})\n        for edge in [None, True, 1, 'ab', {}, [], ['a'], ['a', 'b', 'a']]:\n            cases.append({'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [edge]})\n        for endpoint in [None, False, 0, [], {}, 'unknown', 'A']:\n            cases += [{'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [[endpoint, 'b']]},\n                      {'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', endpoint]]}]\n        cases += [{'nodes': ['a'], 'edges': [['a', 'a']]}, {'nodes': [], 'edges': [['a', 'b']]}]\n        for index, request in enumerate(cases):\n            with self.subTest(case=index):\n                self.invalid(encode(request))\n        escaped = b'{\"nodes\":[\"' + bytes([92]) + b'u0061\",\"b\"],\"edges\":[[\"' + bytes([92]) + b'u0061\",\"b\"]]}'\n        self.valid(escaped, [{'order': ['a', 'b'], 'layers': [['a'], ['b']], 'roots': ['a']}])\n        self.invalid(b'{\"nodes\":[\"a\",\"' + bytes([92]) + b'u0061\"],\"edges\":[]}')\n        self.requests([{'nodes': ['a', 'a0', 'a_', 'a123456789012345'], 'edges': []}])\n\n    def test_strict_json_and_transport(self):\n        base = encode(EMPTY)\n        bad = [b'\\n', b' ', b'\\t\\r\\n', base + b'\\n\\n', base + b'\\n\\n' + base,\n               b'\\n' + base, b'{', base[:-1], base + b' garbage', base + base,\n               b'{\"nodes\":[],\\n\"edges\":[]}', base + b'\\r' + base,\n               b'\\xef\\xbb\\xbf' + base, b'\\xff', base + b'\\n\\xff',\n               b'{\"nodes\":[\"\\xc0\\xaf\"],\"edges\":[]}',\n               b'{\"nodes\":[\"\\xed\\xa0\\x80\"],\"edges\":[]}',\n               b'{\"nodes\":[],\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[]}',\n               b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[],\"edges\":[]}',\n               b'{\"nodes\":[{\"x\":1,\"x\":2}],\"edges\":[]}',\n               b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[{\"x\":1,\"x\":2}]}',\n               b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[],}', b\"{'nodes':[],'edges':[]}\",\n               base + '\\u2028'.encode('utf-8') + base, base + b'\\x0b' + base,\n               b'{\"nodes\":[\"' + bytes([92]) + b'ud800\"],\"edges\":[]}']\n        escaped_key = b'{\"nodes\":[],\"' + bytes([92]) + b'u006eodes\":[],\"edges\":[]}'\n        bad.append(escaped_key)\n        for token in [b'NaN', b'Infinity', b'-Infinity']:\n            bad += [token, b'{\"nodes\":' + token + b',\"edges\":[]}',\n                    b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[],\"extra\":' + token + b'}']\n        bad += [b'{\"nodes\":[' + b'[' * 1500 + b'0' + b']' * 1500 + b'],\"edges\":[]}',\n                b'{\"nodes\":[' + b'9' * 10000 + b'],\"edges\":[]}',\n                b'{\"nodes\":[1e9999],\"edges\":[]}']\n        for index, data in enumerate(bad):\n            with self.subTest(case=index):\n                self.invalid(data)\n        self.valid(b'', [])\n        for index, data in enumerate([base, base + b'\\n', base + b'\\r\\n', b' \\t' + base + b' \\r', base + b'\\r']):\n            with self.subTest(valid_transport=index):\n                self.valid(data, [oracle(EMPTY)])\n        second = {'nodes': ['b', 'a'], 'edges': []}\n        self.valid(base + b'\\r\\n' + encode(second), [oracle(EMPTY), oracle(second)])\n\n    def test_inclusive_limits(self):\n        names = ['n%03d' % i for i in range(120)]\n        distinct = [list(e) for e in itertools.combinations(names, 2)]\n        self.requests([\n            {'nodes': names[::-1], 'edges': []},\n            {'nodes': names, 'edges': [[names[i], names[i + 1]] for i in range(119)]},\n            {'nodes': ['a' * 16], 'edges': []},\n            {'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'b']] * 2000},\n            {'nodes': names, 'edges': distinct[:2000]}])\n        for request in [{'nodes': names + ['n120'], 'edges': []},\n                        {'nodes': ['a' * 17], 'edges': []},\n                        {'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'b']] * 2001},\n                        {'nodes': names, 'edges': distinct[:2001]}]:\n            self.invalid(encode(request))\n        base = encode(EMPTY)\n        for final_lf in [b'', b'\\n']:\n            exact = base + b' ' * (LIMIT - len(base) - len(final_lf)) + final_lf\n            self.assertTrue(len(exact) == LIMIT, 'byte fixture length differs')\n            self.valid(exact, [oracle(EMPTY)])\n            self.invalid(exact + b' ')\n        prefix = base + b'\\n'\n        exact = prefix + base + b' ' * (LIMIT - len(prefix) - len(base))\n        self.valid(exact, [oracle(EMPTY), oracle(EMPTY)])\n        self.invalid(exact + b' ')\n        self.invalid(b' ' * (LIMIT + 1))\n\n    def test_short_reads_and_sentinel(self):\n        reader = self.module['read_bounded']\n        for data, width in [(b'', 1), (encode(EMPTY), 1), (b'x' * LIMIT, 997)]:\n            stream = ShortReader(data, width)\n            self.assertTrue(reader(stream) == data, 'short reads lost input')\n            self.assertTrue(all(0 < size <= LIMIT + 1 for size in stream.requests), 'unbounded acquisition')\n        stream = ShortReader(b'x' * (LIMIT + 20), 997)\n        with self.assertRaises(self.module['InvalidInput']):\n            reader(stream)\n        self.assertTrue(stream.position == LIMIT + 1, 'sentinel consumption differs')\n        self.assertTrue(all(0 < size <= LIMIT + 1 for size in stream.requests), 'unbounded acquisition')\n\n    def test_cycles_and_atomicity(self):\n        cycles = [\n            {'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['b', 'a']]},\n            {'nodes': ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd'], 'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['b', 'c'], ['c', 'd'], ['d', 'a']]},\n            {'nodes': ['a', 'b', 'x', 'y', 'z'], 'edges': [['a', 'b'], ['x', 'y'], ['y', 'z'], ['z', 'x']]}]\n        prefix = encode({'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'b']]}) + b'\\n'\n        suffix = encode(EMPTY) + b'\\n'\n        bad = [encode(r) for r in cycles] + [b'{', b'\\xff', b'',\n               b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[],\"extra\":0}',\n               b'{\"nodes\":[],\"edges\":[],\"nodes\":[]}']\n        for index, line in enumerate(bad):\n            with self.subTest(case=index):\n                self.invalid(prefix + line + b'\\n')\n                self.invalid(line + b'\\n' + suffix)\n                self.invalid(prefix * 40 + line + b'\\n' + suffix)\n        self.requests([EMPTY, {'nodes': ['b', 'a'], 'edges': []}, EMPTY,\n                       {'nodes': ['a', 'b'], 'edges': [['a', 'b']]}])\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    unittest.main(verbosity=1, failfast=True)\n", "BATTERY_COVERAGE.md": "# Batería propuesta, sin ejecución\n\nSe aporta test_topo_plan.py para el argv fijo suministrado. Los fixtures se construyen en memoria. La batería usa únicamente stdlib; carga topo_plan.py junto al test por ruta absoluta con runpy, tanto al importar como en procesos CLI con Python -I -B. No modifica sys.path ni necesita instalación, red o archivos temporales.\n\nCobertura de los criterios originales:\n\n- C01–C03: cero bytes, LF/CRLF y última línea sin terminador; whitespace, líneas vacías, UTF-8 inválido, BOM, sintaxis, claves duplicadas literales y escapadas, constantes no finitas, números enormes y profundidad. Límite inclusivo de 131072 bytes y exceso, también después de peticiones válidas.\n- C04–C05: esquema y tipos, patrón ASCII, nombres escapados, duplicados, extremos desconocidos, pares incorrectos, bucles, 120/121 nodos, 16/17 caracteres y 2000/2001 aristas distintas y duplicadas antes de normalización.\n- C06–C10: expectativas explícitas de los tres ejemplos públicos; cadenas, aislados, convergencias y componentes separados. Oráculo por inspección directa de predecesores restantes, sin heap ni grados incrementales. Todos los grafos dirigidos sin bucles de tres nodos y todas las combinaciones de aristas hacia adelante bajo cada permutación de cuatro nodos; DAG adicionales con semilla fija y variaciones de orden y duplicados. Esquema y tipos de salida, orden del lote y LF final.\n- C09: comprobaciones adicionales sobre las funciones suministradas, repetidas en ambos órdenes, conservando petición, adyacencia y grados originales. Separación de roots y primera ronda.\n- C11: ciclos conectados y desconectados; errores iniciales y tardíos de grafo, JSON y transporte. Cada rechazo comprueba conjuntamente exit 2, stdout vacío y stderr contractual exacto.\n- C12 y V07: importación sin lectura de stdin ni emisión y procesos aislados. Lecturas cortas y consumo del byte centinela reciben fixtures específicos. La batería no acredita por sí sola ausencia universal de acceso externo ni cumplimiento documental, procedural o compatibilidad con todos los intérpretes.\n\nCada proceso tiene timeout de cinco segundos. unittest usa failfast y mensajes breves sin volcar grandes fixtures ni truncar streams. La duración total y el volumen real de diagnóstico no se presentan como mediciones.\n\nEl historial suministra una respuesta anterior de batería, pero no una ejecución ni un recibo de medición. Este contenido no reescribe ese historial. No se aportan cambios a programa, README, criterios originales o configuración.\n\nObservación estática del README suministrado: el diagnóstico literal contractual con LF tiene 24 bytes; README declara 25. La batería exige el literal exacto. La corrección del README queda para el presupuesto posterior de reparación compartido.\n"}}}
